Subject: [PATCH] sycl: DPAS flash attention for quantized KV on Arc A-series (Xe-HPG)

Local candidate. Upstream's DPAS flash-attention kernel (PR 31125: q4_0 / q8_0 KV, 1-31 query
tokens, B580 tg128 at 16K 31.3 -> 54.2 t/s) is fixed to Xe2's 16-wide DPAS and gated to
Battlemage / Lunar Lake / Panther Lake. This makes the DPAS width a template parameter:

- sub-group 16 is upstream's kernel: same operand bytes, same tiles and dispatch;
- sub-group 8 issues dpas (M1, 8) for Xe-HPG: 32 sub-groups per work-group, Q.K over 8-key
  groups, P.V over 8-row tiles, 4 bytes of each A row per lane, 2 keys per lane in the f16 A;
- the width is picked per device at run time: 16 on upstream's allowlist, 8 where the device
  lists the 8x8x32 int8 and 8x8x16 f16 tiles at sub-group 8, else the kernel stays off;
- JIT builds compile both widths into separate device images (the split-K combine kernel runs
  at the same width, so DG2 never builds the (M1, 16) image); spir64_gen builds for one XMX
  width keep that width.

At sub-group 8 the 32-row kernels from head size 128 and the staged D=256 decode kernel spill
in 128 registers on acm-g10 (IGC 2.43), so they always use the 256-register file.
GGML_SYCL_FA_DPAS=0 turns the kernel off, as upstream.

At sub-group 8, Q.K drops the t < RT guard around each s8 / s4 DPAS where the guard is not needed:
with one row tile per job it always holds, and a tile past RT reads in-bounds SLM whose scores the
store discards. On acm-g10 the guard put every Q.K DPAS in its own basic block, and IGC's
Wa_18023229625 issues a dummy DPAS before the first DPAS of each block: the file's 42 sub-group-8
kernels held 490 DPAS and 292 dummies, now 473 and 87 (D = 128, 32 rows: 8 + 8 per job -> 8 + 1;
D = 256 decode: 8 + 8 -> 8 + 0 for q8_0, 8 + 1 for q4_0), with no spills. The guard stays at sub-group 16 (bmg-g21
instruction streams unchanged) and for two-tile jobs at 128 registers, where head size 96 spills
without it. -DGGML_SYCL_FA_DPAS_QK_GUARD=1 keeps it everywhere, the baseline for an A770 A/B.

